(3911172, 549339, 19746, '<td valign="top">Exciting, but the position of the hills/land in the background feel somewhat awkward.  Perhaps a better perspective would have improved the shot?<br/> <br/>You''ve captured a great moment</td>', 'Exciting, but the position of the hills/land in the background feel somewhat awkward.  Perhaps a better perspective would have improved the shot? You''ve captured a great moment', '2007-07-17 17:44:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3911174, 551115, 19746, '<td valign="top">A nice idea with strong colours, although the way the door/slats are structured ends up taking away more from the shot than it ultimately gives.  Your composition is a touch too centred and the gap in the doorway on the left is slightly distracting.<br/> <br/>6 from me - good luck</td>', 'A nice idea with strong colours, although the way the door/slats are structured ends up taking away more from the shot than it ultimately gives.  Your composition is a touch too centred and the gap in the doorway on the left is slightly distracting. 6 from me - good luck', '2007-07-17 17:46:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(3911179, 550145, 19746, '<td valign="top">Dramatic colours and nice composition.  Certainly communicates a dreamlike feeling so you''ve fit the challenge well.  I don''t like how the sail extends above the line of the land although that is completely unavoidable and a minor, personal aesthetic gripe.  <br/> <br/>Maybe a little too heavy handed on the saturation?  A happy medium between the desire to satisfy the conjuration of dreamlike quality (through colour) versus some aversion to the strange pixellation (or artifacting, I''m not sure on what to call it exactly) caused by said oversaturation would have been preferable for my tastes.<br/> <br/>7</td>', 'Dramatic colours and nice composition.  Certainly communicates a dreamlike feeling so you''ve fit the challenge well.  I don''t like how the sail extends above the line of the land although that is completely unavoidable and a minor, personal aesthetic gripe.   Maybe a little too heavy handed on the saturation?  A happy medium between the desire to satisfy the conjuration of dreamlike quality (through colour) versus some aversion to the strange pixellation (or artifacting, I''m not sure on what to call it exactly) caused by said oversaturation would have been preferable for my tastes. 7', '2007-07-17 17:49:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3911186, 552511, 19746, '<td valign="top">Perhaps the surreal nature of the subject would have been a more convincing angle for this one (in the context of the challenge) - nevertheless, this is a really aesthetically pleasing shot.</td>', 'Perhaps the surreal nature of the subject would have been a more convincing angle for this one (in the context of the challenge) - nevertheless, this is a really aesthetically pleasing shot.', '2007-07-17 17:52:01.000000', NULL, 1),
