(3918688, 549885, 66635, '<td valign="top">Beautiful composition.  My only criticism is that the blue sky is too saturated.  It doesn''t look natural.</td>', 'Beautiful composition.  My only criticism is that the blue sky is too saturated.  It doesn''t look natural.', '2007-07-19 14:50:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918751, 552555, 35044, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by piaffe529:</b></div><hr/><i> Did this bomb because I used a little glaus. blur to create a dreamy effect?  I got several OOF remarks, but the original is sharp.  Is it the angle?  I thought it was a neat photo and was hoping to do well, instead it received a 4.9something.<br/> <br/>Any input would be appreciated! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The missing apostrophe?<br/> <br/>The image is certainly pleasant to look at, but lacks a "wow" factor that is necessary (rightly or wrongly) to grab the higher scores here.<br/> <br/>In any photo, one key issue is lighting - good lighting really makes or breaks a photo.  Your photo doesn''t really use lighting to any careful effect.  <br/> <br/>You will have been marked down by some for your soft focus - it is another facet of voting on this site.</td>', 'Originally posted by piaffe529: Did this bomb because I used a little glaus. blur to create a dreamy effect?  I got several OOF remarks, but the original is sharp.  Is it the angle?  I thought it was a neat photo and was hoping to do well, instead it received a 4.9something. Any input would be appreciated!   The missing apostrophe? The image is certainly pleasant to look at, but lacks a "wow" factor that is necessary (rightly or wrongly) to grab the higher scores here. In any photo, one key issue is lighting - good lighting really makes or breaks a photo.  Your photo doesn''t really use lighting to any careful effect.   You will have been marked down by some for your soft focus - it is another facet of voting on this site.', '2007-07-19 15:27:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918770, 552555, 67152, '<td valign="top">It is a pretty horse and you have captured a dream of many a young girls.  However, as others have stated, the image really has some technical issues that resulted in the sub 5 score.  <br/> <br/>First, the lighting is not flattering and works against you - the background is too bright and takes us away from the horse.  Second, the extraneous pole, harness, and other lines distract from the beauty of the horse.  Third, the color cast seems off.  <br/> <br/>I understand that you were trying to use blur to give a feeling of dreaminess - but with the other technical issues, this blur just seemed like OOF.<br/> <br/>Simplifying the image is what is needed for photos on this site to do well - taking a shot of the horse head without the harness and making sure the background does not distract would have scored much better.<br/> <br/></td>', 'It is a pretty horse and you have captured a dream of many a young girls.  However, as others have stated, the image really has some technical issues that resulted in the sub 5 score.   First, the lighting is not flattering and works against you - the background is too bright and takes us away from the horse.  Second, the extraneous pole, harness, and other lines distract from the beauty of the horse.  Third, the color cast seems off.   I understand that you were trying to use blur to give a feeling of dreaminess - but with the other technical issues, this blur just seemed like OOF. Simplifying the image is what is needed for photos on this site to do well - taking a shot of the horse head without the harness and making sure the background does not distract would have scored much better. ', '2007-07-19 15:35:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918798, 552555, 66952, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by piaffe529:</b></div><hr/><i> Did this bomb because I used a little glaus. blur to create a dreamy effect?  I got several OOF remarks, but the original is sharp.  Is it the angle?  I thought it was a neat photo and was hoping to do well, instead it received a 4.9something.<br/> <br/>Any input would be appreciated! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hmmmm....I gave the image a 5, which is close to the average for the image.<br/> <br/>As far as focus goes, when I was voting on this image, I didn''t stop to analyze it, but I remember thinking the blur looked a little strange. Not really out of focus, but not quite right, either. My experience has been in DPC, out of focus images, even if it''s intentional, will get hammered. <br/> <br/>I think the other issue is what Matthew mentioned, the lighting. The combination of lighting and blur makes the horse look pretty flat and lifeless against the bright background. It probably doesn''t help that the horse is just standing there, not doing anything. Maybe a better "dream" picture would have been a dreamy shot of a girl on a horse, galloping across a field.<br/> <br/>I''m not intending to be harsh, because it isn''t that bad of a shot...but these are the things that probably hurt the score. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by piaffe529: Did this bomb because I used a little glaus. blur to create a dreamy effect?  I got several OOF remarks, but the original is sharp.  Is it the angle?  I thought it was a neat photo and was hoping to do well, instead it received a 4.9something. Any input would be appreciated!   hmmmm....I gave the image a 5, which is close to the average for the image. As far as focus goes, when I was voting on this image, I didn''t stop to analyze it, but I remember thinking the blur looked a little strange. Not really out of focus, but not quite right, either. My experience has been in DPC, out of focus images, even if it''s intentional, will get hammered.  I think the other issue is what Matthew mentioned, the lighting. The combination of lighting and blur makes the horse look pretty flat and lifeless against the bright background. It probably doesn''t help that the horse is just standing there, not doing anything. Maybe a better "dream" picture would have been a dreamy shot of a girl on a horse, galloping across a field. I''m not intending to be harsh, because it isn''t that bad of a shot...but these are the things that probably hurt the score.  ', '2007-07-19 15:49:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918821, 552742, 43410, '<td valign="top">this is very nice.  very well done buddy</td>', 'this is very nice.  very well done buddy', '2007-07-19 16:03:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918822, 552555, 19708, '<td valign="top">Rather than duplicate my comments here, take a look in <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=642998" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">your post</a>.</td>', 'Rather than duplicate my comments here, take a look in your post.', '2007-07-19 16:03:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918850, 552977, 30456, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon.  Despite your concerns over the details, I think this is a stunning shot with the ribbon well deserved.  Your artistry with use of the sheets is simply amazing.  The silver tone works perfectly for this.  It''s incredible what you can do pull off at the last minute.</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon.  Despite your concerns over the details, I think this is a stunning shot with the ribbon well deserved.  Your artistry with use of the sheets is simply amazing.  The silver tone works perfectly for this.  It''s incredible what you can do pull off at the last minute.', '2007-07-19 16:18:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918879, 552801, 18450, '<td valign="top">Good concept, great composition...... nice work!!!</td>', 'Good concept, great composition...... nice work!!!', '2007-07-19 16:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3918987, 552977, 31533, '<td valign="top">This is a brilliant piece of work.<br/>I would love to be inside your mind for just one day....</td>', 'This is a brilliant piece of work.I would love to be inside your mind for just one day....', '2007-07-19 17:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3919019, 551031, 64918, '<td valign="top">It''s a DREAM - the over exposure, I''d suggest, is there to give the image an ethereal feel - I think the idea/concept is apt to the challenge, if anything a stronger even contrastier image may have increased the effect. <br/>I think the image has a great deal of potential... maybe try monotone? or just the slightest hint of colour?.. dunno, just kicking around some thoughts.</td>', 'It''s a DREAM - the over exposure, I''d suggest, is there to give the image an ethereal feel - I think the idea/concept is apt to the challenge, if anything a stronger even contrastier image may have increased the effect. I think the image has a great deal of potential... maybe try monotone? or just the slightest hint of colour?.. dunno, just kicking around some thoughts.', '2007-07-19 17:08:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3919048, 550342, 33181, '<td valign="top">Bravo !<br/> <br/>Fastastic piece of work !<br/></td>', 'Bravo ! Fastastic piece of work !', '2007-07-19 17:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3919058, 552555, 44877, '<td valign="top">I''m responding to your post. I gave this a 6 because I liked the dream-like quality of the photo. The title is strange and doesn''t really make sense right off the bat. And there is also a typo. So I''m thinking that people might have been confused. The OOF comments are ridiculous because you clearly meant to have a soft look for this photo.</td>', 'I''m responding to your post. I gave this a 6 because I liked the dream-like quality of the photo. The title is strange and doesn''t really make sense right off the bat. And there is also a typo. So I''m thinking that people might have been confused. The OOF comments are ridiculous because you clearly meant to have a soft look for this photo.', '2007-07-19 17:15:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3920345, 551115, 63398, '<td valign="top">Awesome, Catherine!</td>', 'Awesome, Catherine!', '2007-07-20 00:33:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3921218, 550342, 45559, '<td valign="top">Woooooooooohhhhhhhhhooooooooooooooooooo!!!!!!!! CONGRATS sis, a very well diserved blue. Keep ''em coming! ;)</td>', 'Woooooooooohhhhhhhhhooooooooooooooooooo!!!!!!!! CONGRATS sis, a very well diserved blue. Keep ''em coming! ;)', '2007-07-20 09:59:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3921450, 552245, 17203, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Alley Cat:</b></div><hr/><i>Its not from burning...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If you can explain how it got there, then the SC would be more than willing to reconsider the DQ. Your original had no corresponding detail in that area of the sky.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-20 10:29:13.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Alley Cat:Its not from burning...  If you can explain how it got there, then the SC would be more than willing to reconsider the DQ. Your original had no corresponding detail in that area of the sky.', '2007-07-20 11:28:46.000000', '2007-07-20 11:29:13.000000', 0),
(3921663, 552801, 35044, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by annpatt:</b></div><hr/><i> I know that the usual question in the forums after a challenge is "Why did my shot do so badly?" I don''t have that question this time. My question is  why did this shot do so well?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Given your unusual twist on a common question, it may also be worth putting a twist on the common answer: it did not do all that well.  6.3 is a solid score, but it is not setting the sky on fire.  <br/> <br/>;-)<br/> <br/>FWIW, I like the shot, but the anonymity of the figure does not work so well for me.  Good effort on the bed, though!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-20 12:14:11.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by annpatt: I know that the usual question in the forums after a challenge is "Why did my shot do so badly?" I don''t have that question this time. My question is  why did this shot do so well?  Given your unusual twist on a common question, it may also be worth putting a twist on the common answer: it did not do all that well.  6.3 is a solid score, but it is not setting the sky on fire.   ;-) FWIW, I like the shot, but the anonymity of the figure does not work so well for me.  Good effort on the bed, though!', '2007-07-20 13:13:29.000000', '2007-07-20 13:14:11.000000', 0),
(3921759, 552555, 12268, '<td valign="top">As per you thread...<br/> <br/>There''s a lot going on here &amp; much to look at particularly with the contrast of colours here *horse, straps, etc...).<br/>There isnt one thing that my eye rests on as the focal point when looking at this pic. I dont think the blur tool helped.<br/></td>', 'As per you thread... There''s a lot going on here & much to look at particularly with the contrast of colours here *horse, straps, etc...).There isnt one thing that my eye rests on as the focal point when looking at this pic. I dont think the blur tool helped.', '2007-07-20 13:40:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3922475, 551634, 76430, '<td valign="top">I think you made the right choice here.  The only one of the outtakes that compares is the almost identical one where there is a hint of a smile.  I would like to see her smile more as long as it fits the picture.  I said "Claire?" before because it looked a lot like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=70000" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">lovethelight</a>.  I even went so far as comparing freckles in her portfolio pictures but couldn''t be sure.</td>', 'I think you made the right choice here.  The only one of the outtakes that compares is the almost identical one where there is a hint of a smile.  I would like to see her smile more as long as it fits the picture.  I said "Claire?" before because it looked a lot like  lovethelight.  I even went so far as comparing freckles in her portfolio pictures but couldn''t be sure.', '2007-07-20 17:59:42.000000', NULL, 0);
